chromium-embedded-framework for Debian
======================================

This package builds CEF (Chromium Embedded Framework) using Debian's chromium
source tarball. It requires manual preparation due to the chromium dependency.

================================================================================
BUILD PREREQUISITES
================================================================================

Three dependencies require MANUAL setup before building:

    /path/to/workspace/
    ├── chromium-embedded-framework/          <- This source package
    │   └── depot_tools/                      <- (3) Clone here ONCE
    ├── chromium_143.0.7499.40.orig.tar.xz    <- (1) Chromium source
    └── rust-toolchain.tar.xz                 <- (2) Rust stdlib sources

Setup commands (run ONCE before first build):

1. Chromium tarball (~969 MB):
   $ cd /path/to/workspace/
   $ apt-get source --download-only chromium

   This downloads chromium_VERSION.orig.tar.xz. The CEF branch must match
   the chromium version - see cef/CHROMIUM_BUILD_COMPATIBILITY.txt after
   extracting the source package.

2. Rust toolchain tarball (~142 MB):
   Download from Google Cloud Storage. The URL changes with chromium versions.

   For Chromium 143.x, use:
   $ wget "https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/aspect-aspect-build-toolchain/aspect-aspect-build-toolchain-22.1.128/aspect_build_rust_toolchain_for_x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz" \
          -O rust-toolchain.tar.xz

   For other versions: Extract chromium tarball first, then:
   $ tar -tf chromium_*.orig.tar.xz | grep -i rust | head -5
   $ grep -r "aspect.*rust" chromium/src/DEPS 2>/dev/null | head -5

   Or copy rust-toolchain.tar.xz from a previous successful build.

3. depot_tools (Google's build tools, ~200 MB):
   $ cd chromium-embedded-framework/
   $ git clone https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git depot_tools

   Note: depot_tools is in .gitignore and preserved across builds.
         Its initialization is handled automatically by debian/rules.

4. Build dependencies:
   $ sudo apt install devscripts
   $ cd chromium-embedded-framework/
   $ sudo mk-build-deps -i debian/control

   Or manually install packages listed in debian/control Build-Depends.

Build command:

    $ cd chromium-embedded-framework/
    $ dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

Build time: 30-60 minutes (24-core), 2-4 hours (8-core), 12-24 hours (4-core)
Disk space: ~40 GB
Network: NOT required during build (only for initial setup above)

================================================================================
CONFIGURATION DECISIONS
================================================================================

1. SYSTEM LIBC++ (use_custom_libcxx=false)
------------------------------------------

Decision: Use Debian's libc++-19-dev instead of bundled libc++
Reason: Aligns with Debian Chromium's approach
Implementation: GN flag use_custom_libcxx=false in debian/rules

2. SYSTEM LLVM/CLANG (clang-19)
-------------------------------

Decision: Use Debian's clang-19 toolchain
Reason: Standard Debian build practice, no bundled compiler
Implementation: clang_base_path="/usr/lib/llvm-19" in debian/rules

Note: LLVM version is locked to 19. When Debian updates to a new LLVM version,
update CLANG_MVERS in debian/rules and patch 0012 (see "Updating LLVM Version").

3. DEPOT_TOOLS (Manual Clone Required)
--------------------------------------

Decision: Require manual clone of Google's depot_tools
Reason: Not available as Debian package, required by CEF build system
Implementation: User clones to depot_tools/ directory (in .gitignore)

Setup: git clone https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git depot_tools
Note: Clone ONCE, then preserved across builds. Initialization is automatic.

depot_tools is a BUILD TOOL only - nothing from it is installed in binary packages.

Future: When/if depot_tools becomes a Debian package, add to Build-Depends.

4. BUNDLED RUST STDLIB SOURCES
------------------------------

Decision: Use rust-toolchain.tar.xz for Rust standard library sources
Reason: Debian's rust-src (1.90.0) lacks files Chromium requires
Implementation: debian/rules extracts library/ from tarball

Future: When Debian rust-src includes all required files, switch to system
rust-src and remove tarball requirement.

================================================================================
INTERIM DEPENDENCIES DETAILS
================================================================================

This section provides technical details for the interim workarounds. These
will become unnecessary when proper Debian packages are available.

Rust Toolchain Tarball
----------------------

Location: ../rust-toolchain.tar.xz (parent directory of source package)
Size: ~142 MB
Contents: Rust standard library sources matching Chromium's expected version

See BUILD PREREQUISITES section for download instructions.

What debian/rules does with it (Step 7e):
- Extracts ONLY library/ directory to third_party/rust-toolchain/lib/rustlib/src/rust/
- Creates stubs for cross-platform files (cygwin, darwin) needed for module resolution

LLVM-19 Path Configuration
--------------------------

Chromium's GN build system uses rust_bindgen_root to find both:
- bindgen executable: ${rust_bindgen_root}/bin/bindgen
- libclang library: ${rust_bindgen_root}/lib/libclang.so

On Debian:
- bindgen is at /usr/bin/bindgen (rust_bindgen_root="/usr" works)
- libclang is at /usr/lib/llvm-19/lib/ (NOT /usr/lib/)

Solution: Patch 0012-bindgen-libclang-abspath.chromium.patch intercepts
/usr/lib and redirects to /usr/lib/llvm-19/lib where libclang actually exists.

Files affected by LLVM version:
- debian/control: clang-19, lld-19, libc++-19-dev, etc.
- debian/rules: CLANG_MVERS := 19
- debian/patches/chromium/0012-*: hardcoded /usr/lib/llvm-19/lib

Depot Tools Initialization
--------------------------

debian/rules automatically handles depot_tools setup:

Step 6.6.0.5 - Initialize if needed:
- Checks for python3_bin_reldir.txt (initialization marker)
- Runs ./update_depot_tools if missing

Step 6.6.0.6 - Python symlink:
- depot_tools expects bundled Python at bootstrap-2@*/python3/bin/python3
- Creates symlink to system /usr/bin/python3

No manual action required - these run automatically during build.

Build Environment Notes
-----------------------

The build is designed to work WITHOUT network access once tarballs are in place.
debian/rules handles all environment setup automatically:

- Adds /usr/lib/llvm-19/bin to PATH (for clang discovery)
- Sets LIBCLANG_PATH=/usr/lib/llvm-19/lib (for bindgen)
- Initializes depot_tools with system Python
- Uses full path to autoninja (patch 0016) to avoid PATH issues

================================================================================
PATCHES
================================================================================

CEF Patches (debian/patches/*.cef.patch)
----------------------------------------

Applied via quilt to CEF source before build:

- 0001-debian-patcher-skip-logic: Skip upstream patches already in Debian chromium
- 0002-use-system-clang: Use system clang instead of downloading
- 0003-create-reclient-stub: Stub for Google's build cache (not used in Debian)
- 0004-patch-gn-for-exec-script: Allow CEF's exec_script in GN
- 0005-skip-gclient-revert-debian: Don't revert Debian's chromium patches
- 0006-skip-chromium-checkout-debian: Use tarball instead of git checkout
- 0007-allow-optimize-webui-false: Allow disabling WebUI optimization
- 0008-add-locale-stub-for-protoc-gen-js: Locale stub for JS proto generation
- 0010-add-rust-toolchain-stub: Use system Rust instead of downloading
- 0011-fix-opus-stub-after-gclient: Fix opus configuration
- 0012-add-gn-debian-args-function: Inject Debian GN args
- 0013-remove-pseudolocales-conditional: Fix locale generation
- 0014-disable-assert-redefinition: Avoid macro conflicts with system headers
- 0015-add-debian-cef-rpath-for-angle: RPATH for ANGLE libraries
- 0016-use-full-path-autoninja-dpkg: Fix autoninja discovery in build

Chromium Patches (debian/patches/chromium/*.chromium.patch)
-----------------------------------------------------------

Applied manually via patch -p1 to chromium source:

- 0012-bindgen-libclang-abspath: Fix libclang path for rust-bindgen
  (redirects /usr/lib to /usr/lib/llvm-19/lib)

See debian/rules for the complete list of chromium patches.

================================================================================
MAINTENANCE
================================================================================

Updating CEF Version
--------------------

1. Update CEF_BRANCH in debian/rules
2. Update chromium version to match CEF requirements
3. Test build and fix any new patch conflicts

Updating Chromium Version
-------------------------

1. Download new chromium tarball: apt-get source --download-only chromium
2. Update version in debian/rules --chromium-archive path
3. Test build and fix any patch conflicts

Updating LLVM Version
---------------------

When Debian moves to a new LLVM version (e.g., 19 -> 20):

1. Update debian/control Build-Depends (clang-19 -> clang-20, etc.)
2. Update CLANG_MVERS in debian/rules (19 -> 20)
3. Update debian/patches/chromium/0012-bindgen-libclang-abspath.chromium.patch
   (change /usr/lib/llvm-19/lib to /usr/lib/llvm-20/lib)
4. Test build for new compiler warnings/errors

================================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

Common Issues
-------------

1. "chromium tarball not found"
   -> Run: apt-get source --download-only chromium (in parent directory)

2. "rust-toolchain.tar.xz not found"
   -> Download from GCS URL in chromium DEPS file (see BUILD PREREQUISITES)

3. "Unable to find libclang"
   -> Verify libclang1-19 is installed (pulled in by clang-19)
   -> Check patch 0012 has correct LLVM version

4. "Command 'autoninja' not found"
   -> Patch 0016 should fix this; verify it's in debian/patches/series

5. "depot_tools directory not found"
   -> Clone depot_tools: git clone https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git depot_tools

6. Disk space errors
   -> Build requires ~40GB free space

Checklist for New Build Machines
--------------------------------

[ ] Chromium tarball: ../chromium_143.0.7499.40.orig.tar.xz
[ ] Rust toolchain: ../rust-toolchain.tar.xz
[ ] depot_tools cloned: ./depot_tools/ (git clone once)
[ ] Build dependencies: apt build-dep chromium-embedded-framework
[ ] Sufficient disk space (~40GB)

================================================================================
FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS
================================================================================

When these Debian packages become available, this package can be simplified:

1. chromium-source package (Bug #893448)
   -> Remove manual chromium tarball requirement

2. depot-tools package
   -> Remove bundled depot_tools, add to Build-Depends

3. Updated rust-src package
   -> Remove rust-toolchain.tar.xz requirement

